DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The wwccssccmmpp() function is the wide‐character equivalent of the ssttrrccmmpp(3)
       function.   It  compares the wide‐character string pointed to by _s_1 and
       the wide‐character string pointed to by _s_2.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The wwccssccmmpp() function returns zero if the wide‐character strings at  _s_1
       and  _s_2  are  equal.  It returns an integer greater than zero if at the
       first differing position _i, the corresponding wide‐character  _s_1_[_i_]  is
       greater  than  _s_2_[_i_].   It  returns an integer less than zero if at the
       first differing position _i, the corresponding wide‐character  _s_1_[_i_]  is
       less than _s_2_[_i_].

